-- title:
--   Degeneracy values j(qᵈ) read off j(E/H[d])
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N$ a nonzero natural number with $N \neq 0$ in $K$, let $k$ and $\Omega$ be fields (with decidable equality on $\Omega$) carrying $K$-algebra structures and a $k$-algebra structure on $\Omega$ forming a tower $K \to k \to \Omega$, and let $E$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ whose $j$-invariant is transcendental over $K$, such that the $N$-torsion of the affine point group of $E_\Omega$ has cardinality exactly $N^2$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` for the intermediate field of $K$ in the Laurent series field over $K$ generated by all substitutions $q \mapsto q^d$, $d \mid N$, $d \neq 0$, of the series $j(q) = q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$, that is `jqModC K`. Then there is a bijection $\Phi$ from the set of subgroups $H$ of $E_\Omega(\Omega)$ that are additively cyclic with $\mathrm{card}\,H = N$ onto the set of $K$-algebra homomorphisms $\psi : F \to \Omega$ with $\psi(j(q)) = j(E)$ (image under $k \to \Omega$), with the following two properties. First, equivariance: for every $k$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\Omega$ and all such $H, H'$ with $H'$ the image of $H$ under the map on points induced by $\sigma$, one has $\Phi(H') = \sigma \circ \Phi(H)$ (with $\sigma$ restricted to a $K$-algebra map). Second, for every algebraically closed field $L$ with decidable equality that is a $k$- and $\Omega$-algebra forming a tower $k \to \Omega \to L$, every such $H$, every nonzero $d \mid N$ and every subgroup $H' \le H$ of $E_\Omega(\Omega)$ that is additively cyclic of cardinality $d$, the image in $L$ of $\Phi(H)$ applied to the substituted series $j(q^d) =$ `jqNModC K d` equals `(E.baseChange L).cyclicQuotientJ` of the image of $H'$ under the point map induced by $\Omega \to L$, at parameter $d$ — namely $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the Weierstrass curve produced by the `cqjIterate` construction, i.e. the $j$-invariant of the quotient of $E_L$ by that image.
--
--   This is the canonical moduli dictionary for $X_0(N)$ in its full presentation: the $K$-algebra maps out of the field generated by all degeneracy expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$, normalised by $j(q) \mapsto j(E)$, correspond Galois-equivariantly to cyclic subgroups of order $N$ on $E$, and each intermediate degeneracy value $j(q^d)$ is computed by the quotient of $E$ by the order-$d$ subgroup of the level structure (the cases $d = N$ and $d = 1$ being the defining normalisations). It extends the statement for $j(q^N)$ alone and is used in the construction of moduli places and moduli test data for $X_0(N)$.
